index 28b0891..32ee3d0 100644
--- a/saas/README.md
+++ b/saas/README.md
@@ -24,6 +24,25 @@ After making changes to this gem, you need to update Fizzy to pick up the change
 BUNDLE_GEMFILE=Gemfile.saas bundle update --conservative fizzy-saas
 ```
 
+## Billing
+
+Hosted Fizzy is free for 1,000 cards and 1 GB of storage. Beyond that, accounts subscribe to a paid plan through Stripe:
+
+| Plan       | Price     | Cards     | Storage |
+|------------|-----------|-----------|---------|
+| Free       | —         | 1,000     | 1 GB    |
+| Unlimited  | $20/month | unlimited | 5 GB    |
+| Unlimited+ | $25/month | unlimited | 500 GB  |
+
+The price list lives in `app/models/plan.rb`. Stripe hosts the checkout and the customer portal, and posts subscription changes to `/stripe/webhooks`, which `Account::Subscription` mirrors. That takes these environment variables, provided by the deploys (`config/deploy.*.yml`) and locally by `stripe-dev` (below):
+
+* `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY` and `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET`
+* `STRIPE_MONTHLY_V1_PRICE_ID` (Unlimited) and `STRIPE_MONTHLY_EXTRA_STORAGE_V1_PRICE_ID` (Unlimited+)
+
+A free account that runs out of cards can still draft, but publishing and creating cards through the API are refused until it upgrades. Admins see their plan and an upgrade in the account settings.
+
+Support tools are in the admin area, for staff: `/admin/accounts` lists the accounts, and each account's page can comp it (a paid plan without the bill) and override its card count and bytes used to stand in for the real usage when checking limits. Storage exceptions (`Account#add_storage_exception`) raise an account's storage allowance from the console.
+
 ## Working with Stripe
 
 The first time, you need to:
